# Agent Subagent Lifecycle

Spec: SubagentLifecycle
Purpose:
  Define the sub-agent pyramid lifecycle for the SW1 swarm chain:
  spawn depth cap, self-delegation, single-writer code ownership,
  typed-outcome-to-STATE notification, runtime folders, cleanup
  precondition, state-driven dispatch trigger, and the RECONCILE
  gate that runs before every DISPATCH.

Owns: agent/subagent-lifecycle.sdd

Source: DEC-2026-1011-002 (D3), extends agent/supervisor.sdd + agent/coordination.sdd

Levels:
  L0: supervisor — orchestrates the task graph, never executes.
  L1: stage-agent — dispatched per macro-stage; may spawn L2 children.
  L2: sub-agent — executes one micro-unit; MUST NOT spawn further agents.
  SPAWN DEPTH CAP = 2 levels below L0 (L0 -> L1 -> L2). L2 is terminal.

Spawn:
  Self-delegation: an L1 agent that receives an over-budget or
  decomposable unit subdivides it and spawns L2 sub-agents ITSELF.
  Every sub-unit keeps the full MICRO-UNIT budget (<=1 file, <=150
  line diff, <=8k token pack, 1 subagent step). Subdivision re-runs
  DECOMPOSE with finer granularity until the budget holds or the unit
  is atomic.

CodeOwnership:
  Single-writer per scope: a sub-agent writes code inside its
  path-locked scope. The parent MUST NEVER edit a child's locked
  scope. Scope lock is per MU-XXX; concurrent parallel units never
  share mutable state.

Notification:
  Typed outcome written to STATE only. Outcome vocabulary:
    SUCCESS | PARTIAL | BLOCKED | NEEDS_CLARIFICATION |
    POLICY_VIOLATION | TOOL_ERROR | UNSAFE
  Agent-to-agent messaging is FORBIDDEN; a consumer reads STATE.

Folder:
  Path: .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/agents/{agent_id}/
  Holds: context pack + outcome record + evidence artifacts.
  Runtime-only; never committed ([R103]).

Cleanup:
  Folder deleted only when the unit is DONE + VERIFIED with zero
  open attributed defects. Prefer re-verify over destructive
  cleanup; a live RUNNING entry is never deleted on suspicion.

Trigger:
  Dependent units (depends_on) become dispatchable when their
  dependency reaches DONE. This is a STATE transition, never a
  message. Channel routing (R sequential / F concurrent) is derived
  per dispatch-channels.sdd.

Reconciliation:
  Every /sdd-swarm invocation runs RECONCILE before DISPATCH:
    1. read the sub-agent registry;
    2. verify parent_id ownership per entry;
    3. re-verify or defect-catalog orphaned RUNNING entries;
    4. delete stale folders (DONE + VERIFIED + no open defect).
  New dispatch is BLOCKED until the registry is clean or explicitly
  waived. Re-verify is preferred over destructive cleanup.

Rules:
  [SAL1] Depth cap 2 — L2 sub-agents MUST NOT spawn further agents.
  [SAL2] Spawning is self-delegation — an agent subdivides its OWN
        over-budget unit and spawns its children itself.
  [SAL3] Single-writer per scope — a parent MUST NOT edit a child's
        locked scope.
  [SAL4] Notification is typed-outcome-to-STATE only — agent-to-agent
        messaging is forbidden.
  [SAL5] Every agent has a runtime folder under
        .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/agents/{agent_id}/ with context pack
        + outcome + evidence.
  [SAL6] Folder cleanup requires the unit DONE + VERIFIED + zero open
        attributed defects.
  [SAL7] Dependent units become dispatchable via STATE transition
        (dependency DONE) — never via messages.
  [SAL8] RECONCILE runs before every DISPATCH: registry ownership
        check, orphan re-verify, stale-folder cleanup; dispatch
        blocked until clean or explicitly waived.

